[Note: I got this game for free because I won it; not because it was given to me by a developer.]
As you probably realize by now, this game is a series of logic puzzles.  There is a Stanley Parable-esque section in middle of the game that provides some humor, a tiny bit of "story," and most importantly a little break for your brain.  And there are a few Easter egg type things to discover in the game.
It's very simple:  if you like logic puzzles, then you'll like this game.  If you don't, or lack the patience or skill to solve them, then you won't.  :)
Most of the people who downvoted this game did so for one or more of the following reasons:
- They don't like logic puzzles;
- They were unable to solve the puzzles logically;
- They thought the game was "too short" because when they couldn't immediately figure out a solution, they just guessed until they were right.  [There's no penalty for a wrong selection; you just are presented with the same puzzle.]
- They we unimpressed by the middle section and thought it should be longer, more interesting, or otherwise different;
- They are offended by the fact that there is an apparently unattainable achievement just to mess with completionists (like myself).
As a completionist, I don't love the apparently unattainable achievement that a year later nobody has figured out.  But I can forgive it; there might even be a solution if somebody is determined (or lucky) enough to find it.

